{% comment %}
  sections/featured-offer.liquid

  One offer over a photograph: a panel on one side, highlight cards on the
  other, and a strip of details under both.

  ## Why it is not a subscription section

  It was drawn as one, and the Theme Store requirements are the reason it is
  not. Subscriptions there are the Selling Plan API — a merchant creates selling
  plans and the theme has to show the selected plan through to the cart. This
  section has no part in that: its options are links, so a strip that said
  "Every month / Every 2 months" would advertise a purchase flow the section
  cannot carry out, and the customer would arrive at a page with nothing
  subscribed.

  So the option chooser stayed and the subscription vocabulary went. A merchant
  whose store does sell subscriptions can label the options however their app
  requires and point each one at the right page; every other merchant gets a
  chooser for sizes, tiers, bundles or plans. The section is honest about being
  a promotion either way.

  The same requirement is why the preset carries no ratings, review counts or
  customer totals. Fabricated figures are listed there as false data and claims,
  alongside fake countdowns and stock levels, and a number a merchant has to
  remember to go and delete is a number some store will ship.

  ## The shell is `sections/main-faq.liquid`'s, setting id for setting id

  Container, colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the two
  radii, the margins, the layout vocabulary and the gaps — every id here is one
  that section already carries, and both reach them through
  `snippets/spacing.liquid`, `snippets/background-media.liquid` and
  `snippets/container.liquid` rather than reimplementing any of it. A merchant
  who has arranged an FAQ section has arranged this one.

  What it adds is a minimum height. A panel over a photograph is a hero, and a
  hero sized only by its content is as tall as whichever paragraph the merchant
  last edited. The two sliders are a floor, not a height: the section still
  grows when the content needs more room.

  ## The background drifts, and it is never an empty box

  Parallax is `snippets/background-image.liquid`'s, reached by two settings the
  Group block already carries. It stands down on touch and under
  `prefers-reduced-motion`, and it is one shared ticker rather than a scroll
  listener per section.

  The placeholder is the other half of the same idea. A section whose whole
  subject is a photograph should show the shape of one before anything is
  uploaded, so `background-media` is asked for a placeholder here — the panel
  lands on a picture-shaped box in the editor rather than on the colour scheme,
  and the merchant can see the layout they are filling in.

  ## The option chooser is `blocks/tabs.liquid`, not a control of its own

  Several options, one selected, and a button under the selected one that goes
  to that option's page. That is a tablist with one panel each, so it is the
  theme's tab block set to **Segmented** with a **Button** block inside each
  tab, and the keyboard behaviour, the sliding marker, the ARIA and the whole
  button system come with it.

  Three things were added to the tab blocks to make it, and each is generic:

    Segmented           `blocks/tabs.liquid` — the filled track and the options
                        sharing its width. A Monthly/Yearly switch wants it too.
    A flag on a tab     `blocks/_tab.liquid` — a short word above an option.
                        It ships empty; it is the merchant's to write.
    The tab that opens  `blocks/_tab.liquid` — so the option a merchant leads
                        with need not be the one listed first, which would
                        change the order a customer reads and a keyboard walks.

  ## Everything else is blocks the theme already had

  The panel is a **Card content** with a background and a border. The label is a
  **Subheading**, the heading and the paragraph are **Text**, the cards are
  **Badge highlight** and the short notes are **Icon with text**. The preset
  wires them together; none of them knows it is in this section.

  That is also why the layout controls matter more than they look. The section
  is a flex container of its own children, so the panel sits beside the cards
  because they are siblings — not because a selector went looking for them —
  and a merchant who deletes one is left with a section that still lays out
  rather than one with a hole in it.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    The background is the colour scheme's until the merchant says otherwise:
    either a colour of their own, or a picture behind the whole section.

    The colour is emitted as a real `background` declaration rather than a
    custom property because `color-scheme-container` paints a background *and* a
    gradient image, and only the shorthand clears both.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    One width per side rather than one for the box, summed into `border_any` so
    the three properties are emitted only when at least one side is drawn — a
    zero-width border with a colour on it is three declarations that paint
    nothing.

    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the offer along with its frame. With no colour picked the
    border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters cannot take an alpha
    channel from, so `color-mix` does the same fade in the browser instead and
    both paths honour the slider.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners and margins ----

    A phone gets its own radius because the same number does not read the same
    at both widths — 40px is a soft lift across 1400px and a heavy scoop out of
    a 390px screen. `| default: radius` rather than a constant, so a section
    saved before the mobile slider existed keeps one shape at every width.
  endcomment
  assign radius = s.border_radius | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign radius_mobile = s.border_radius_mobile | default: radius | plus: 0
  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the floor ----

    A minimum, not a height. The section grows past it whenever the content
    needs the room, so a merchant who adds a fourth promise to the panel gets a
    taller section rather than a scrollbar inside one.

    Zero is the off switch and is what an untouched section carries, which is
    why this is emitted unconditionally: `min-block-size: 0px` is what the box
    would do anyway, so there is no state where writing it changes a layout that
    was not asking for it.

    The phone falls back to the desktop number rather than to a constant. A hero
    900px tall on a laptop is most of a phone screen, so the two are nearly
    always different — but a section saved before the mobile slider existed
    should keep the one height it was given.
  endcomment
  assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign min_height_mobile = s.min_height_mobile | default: min_height | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- layout ----

    The Group block's vocabulary rather than a second one invented here:
    Alignment is always the horizontal axis and Position always the vertical,
    and `assets/base.css` decides which CSS property reads which from the
    direction. `snippets/group.liquid` sets out why that swap lives in one
    place.

    This file does not guess which child is which. Horizontal is a flex row of
    the section's own children, so the offer panel and the proof cards sit side
    by side because they are siblings.
  endcomment
  assign direction = s.direction | default: 'row'
  assign is_row = false
  if direction == 'row'
    assign is_row = true
  endif

  comment
    Two settings, one control. The horizontal list carries the distribution
    options on top of the three alignments, because on a row they land on the
    same `justify-content` and only one of the two could win. On a column they
    would be inert, so that list is the plain three and the merchant never sees
    an option that does nothing.
  endcomment
  if is_row
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment_row | default: 'start'
  else
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment | default: 'start'
  endif

  case alignment_setting
    when 'center'
      assign alignment_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign alignment_axis = 'end'
    else
      assign alignment_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    The alignment with the distribution folded in, and the plain one beside it.
    They differ exactly when a distribution is chosen, and the phone stack needs
    the plain one: `space-between` is valid on the `justify-content` it feeds on
    a desktop row and invalid on the `align-items` it would feed once stacked.
  endcomment
  assign inline_axis = alignment_axis
  if is_row
    case alignment_setting
      when 'space-between', 'space-around', 'space-evenly'
        assign inline_axis = alignment_setting
    endcase
  endif

  comment
    `stretch` is offered here and not on the FAQ's list because this section's
    two columns are panels rather than runs of text: an offer panel that ends
    where its paragraph ends, beside a taller column of proof cards, reads as an
    unfinished box. It is the vertical axis, so it only ever reaches
    `align-items`, where `stretch` is valid.
  endcomment
  case s.position
    when 'center'
      assign block_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign block_axis = 'end'
    when 'stretch'
      assign block_axis = 'stretch'
    else
      assign block_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    ---- the gaps ----

    A Desktop/Mobile pair behind one switch, the shape every other section in
    the theme uses. Both pairs are published unconditionally and
    `assets/base.css` picks which applies at a given width, because the pair the
    merchant is not looking at in the editor is still the pair the other
    breakpoint renders.

    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone, which would replace a deliberate 0 —
    a gap a merchant can legitimately want when the panel is meant to sit flush
    against the cards beside it. Each mobile axis falls back to its desktop
    value when the setting is absent entirely, so a section saved before the
    mobile pair existed renders as it did; one added since gets the schema
    default, which is half the desktop one.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 24 | plus: 0
  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | default: gap_x | plus: 0
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | default: gap_y | plus: 0

  assign content_classes = 'featured-offer__content featured-offer__content--' | append: direction
  if is_row and s.stack_on_mobile
    assign content_classes = content_classes | append: ' featured-offer__content--stack-mobile'
  endif

  comment
    Reverse is `flex-direction: row-reverse`, not a second ordering of the
    blocks — the markup stays in the order a screen reader and a keyboard read
    it, and only the paint order changes. That is also why it is row-only: a
    reversed *column* would put the guarantees above the offer for everybody
    using the page without sight of it.

    What it is for is the mirrored arrangement, where the photograph's subject
    is on the other side of the frame and the panel has to move off it. Which
    side is a design decision rather than a rebuild, so it is a checkbox and not
    a second preset that would need every change made to it twice.
  endcomment
  if is_row and s.reverse
    assign content_classes = content_classes | append: ' featured-offer__content--reverse'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture content_style -%}
  --featured-offer-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --featured-offer-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --featured-offer-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --featured-offer-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --featured-offer-inline: {{ inline_axis }};
  --featured-offer-align: {{ alignment_axis }};
  --featured-offer-block: {{ block_axis }};
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --featured-offer-radius: {{ radius }}px;
  --featured-offer-radius-mobile: {{ radius_mobile }}px;
  --featured-offer-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --featured-offer-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  --featured-offer-min-height: {{ min_height }}px;
  --featured-offer-min-height-mobile: {{ min_height_mobile }}px;
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --featured-offer-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --featured-offer-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --featured-offer-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="featured-offer color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    `priority: true` because this section is a hero and a hero is above the
    fold. A lazy background here is the largest paint on the page arriving after
    everything around it, which is the one picture in a theme worth loading
    eagerly.

    `placeholder` is opt-in in `background-media`, and this is a section that
    wants it: the whole layout is a panel read against a photograph, so before
    one is uploaded the merchant should be looking at a picture-shaped box
    rather than at flat scheme colour with the panel floating on it. It is drawn
    only when Image is the chosen background and none has been picked — a
    merchant who wants no picture chooses None and gets nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media',
       settings: s,
       priority: true,
       placeholder: 'hero-apparel-1' %}
  {%- endif -%}
  

  <div class="featured-offer__inner {% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      `children: true` staggers the direct children — the offer panel, then the
      proof cards, then the guarantees — so the section arrives as one cascade
      rather than as a wall that appears at once. The stagger is a setting; at
      its default of 0 they simply arrive together.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <motion-effect
      class="{{ content_classes }}"
      data-easing="outQuint"
      style="{{ content_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
      {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
    >
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
    </motion-effect>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.featured_offer.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "@theme"
    },
    {
      "type": "@app"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "edge",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "wide",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "standard",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "compact",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "custom",
          "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "column",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "row",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "row"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "reverse",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.reverse.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.reverse.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "stack_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'column' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment_row",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-between",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-around",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "space-evenly",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "position",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "start",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "center",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "end",
          "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__3.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "stretch",
          "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.position.options__4.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap_device",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "desktop",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "mobile",
          "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 24,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_offer.headers.height"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_offer.paragraphs.height"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1000,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height_mobile.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1000,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.appearance.header"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "none",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "image",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "video",
          "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__3.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.color.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "cover",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label"
        },
        {
          "value": "fit",
          "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label"
        }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
